# NOT TRANSLATED (see meta.json: classification "not-expressible"). `_NS =
# Namespace(...)` here is a required class attribute of a `DefinedNamespace`
# subclass, not a lexical vocabulary shortcut: rdflib's own
# `DefinedNamespaceMeta.__getitem__` reads `cls._NS` at attribute-access
# time. Replacing this line with `@prefix rbdyn_coord: <...> .` removes the
# `_NS` class attribute entirely (`@prefix` is a transpile-time lexical
# binding, not a runtime value/attribute), and every subsequent
# `RBDYN_COORD.Whatever` access breaks with
# `AttributeError: DefinedNamespace like object has no attribute '_NS'`
